From: WallView
Subject: [PATCH] Coordinated graphics: do not block the compositor on tiles
 that are still being painted

CoordinatedPlatformLayer::flushCompositingState() took the pending
backing store update of a layer and CoordinatedBackingStoreTile then
waited for every tile buffer that was not finished: for the painting
thread (waitUntilPaintingComplete()) and for the GPU (serverWait() on
the fence of the tile). While scrolling a Home Assistant dashboard on the
NSPanel every main thread commit with new tiles stopped the compositor
for 4-50 ms, so the frames with the new scroll position missed their
vblank.

Leave the pending update of a layer in its proxy while one of its tile
buffers is not painted or its fence has not signaled, compose the frame
with the tiles the layer already has and schedule another composition.
The update of a layer is still applied as a whole, and after two
deferred frames the compositor waits as before, so content cannot be
starved by continuous repaints. Pending damage is kept with the deferred
update.

WALLVIEW_WEBKIT_TILE_DEFER=<frames> sets the limit of deferred frames
(default 2); 0 waits for every tile as before, for A/B measurements.

Upstream-Status: Pending
